## Scenarios

### authenticated decryption must reject any tampered ciphertext

#### each tampered variant really differs from the original token

- Verify: each tampered variant really differs from the original token
   - Expected: _really_tampered_count() equals `3`


<details>
<summary>Executable SSpec</summary>

Runnable source: 3 lines folded for reproduction.
Reproduction: this block contains the complete executable scenario source.

```simple
# @req: REQ-SSPEC-LOCAL-001
step("Verify: each tampered variant really differs from the original token")
expect(_really_tampered_count()).to_equal(3)
```

</details>

#### no tampered variant is accepted, in the nonce, ciphertext or MAC region

- Verify: no tampered variant is accepted, in the nonce, ciphertext or MAC region
   - Expected: _accepted_tamper_count() equals `0`


<details>
<summary>Executable SSpec</summary>

Runnable source: 3 lines folded for reproduction.
Reproduction: this block contains the complete executable scenario source.

```simple
step("Verify: no tampered variant is accepted, in the nonce, ciphertext or MAC region")
# @req: REQ-SSPEC-LOCAL-001
expect(_accepted_tamper_count()).to_equal(0)
```

</details>

#### the untampered token still decrypts, so rejection is not blanket

- Verify: the untampered token still decrypts, so rejection is not blanket
   - Expected: _decrypt_ok(_token_text()) is true


<details>
<summary>Executable SSpec</summary>

Runnable source: 3 lines folded for reproduction.
Reproduction: this block contains the complete executable scenario source.

```simple
step("Verify: the untampered token still decrypts, so rejection is not blanket")
# @req: REQ-SSPEC-LOCAL-001
expect(_decrypt_ok(_token_text())).to_equal(true)
```

</details>

#### the untampered token decrypts to the exact original plaintext

- Verify: the untampered token decrypts to the exact original plaintext
   - Expected: _decrypted_text() equals `_plaintext()`


<details>
<summary>Executable SSpec</summary>

Runnable source: 3 lines folded for reproduction.
Reproduction: this block contains the complete executable scenario source.

```simple
step("Verify: the untampered token decrypts to the exact original plaintext")
# @req: REQ-SSPEC-LOCAL-001
expect(_decrypted_text()).to_equal(_plaintext())
```

</details>

